/**
\page tbs ☀️ The Broken Seal

\htmlonly<p class="game-banner game-tbs"><span class="mark">&#x2600;&#xFE0F;</span>Golden Sun: The Broken Seal, built entirely from <code>games/tbs</code>. Code inside <code>#if</code> follows the English edition (<code>TBS_EDITION_EN</code>): what only another edition builds, such as the Spanish and Italian <code>System_GetLanguage</code>, is in the source files but not on these pages.</p>\endhtmlonly

The questions people bring, and where each is answered:
- Where is the code for a move? \ref tbs_abilities "Abilities" names the
  function that plays it; \ref how-to-find-an-effect "Finding an effect" shows
  how to read and change it.
- How does a battle run, from the first menu to the spoils?
  \ref how-a-battle-runs "How a battle runs".
- How much damage does a move do, and what decides it?
  \ref how-an-ability-resolves "How an ability resolves".
- Where does something happen in a town or dungeon? \ref tbs_places "Places"
  names the scene; \ref how-to-find-a-scene-and-an-event-in-it "Finding a scene and an event in it"
  finds the event, and \ref how-a-scene-runs "How a scene runs" explains it.
- How does a field Psynergy such as Move or Reveal work?
  \ref how-to-find-a-field-psynergy "Finding a field Psynergy".
- How do I change a menu screen or a shop?
  \ref how-to-change-a-screen "Changing a menu screen" and
  \ref how-to-change-a-counter "Changing a shop counter".

Each folder of the code has a guide, grouped by what it covers, and each
links to its folder under Source:

- \subpage guide_world
- \subpage guide_battle
- \subpage guide_menus
- \subpage tbs_game
- \subpage guide_engine

To find code by what you see in the game:

- \subpage tbs_places lists every place, with what happens there.
- \subpage tbs_abilities lists every ability with an effect of its own, and
  the function that plays it.

For the matching underneath:

- \subpage tbs_marks lists every original bug, dead branch and compiler
  device, each linked to its line.
- \subpage tbs_asm lists the assembly that is code rather than a picture's
  wrapper.
- \subpage tbs_matching explains how the build is judged and what the markers in the code mean.

In the cartridge the code sits in one bank per folder, in this order:
\ref games/tbs/src/runtime "runtime", \ref games/tbs/src/field "field",
\ref games/tbs/src/window "window", \ref games/tbs/src/game "game",
\ref games/tbs/src/menu "menu", \ref games/tbs/src/shop "shop",
\ref games/tbs/src/battle "battle", \ref games/tbs/src/effect "effect" and
\ref games/tbs/src/object "object", beside \ref games/tbs/src/graphics "graphics",
maps, \ref games/tbs/src/sound "sound", \ref games/tbs/src/system "system",
\ref games/tbs/src/debug "debug" and \ref games/tbs/src/scene "scene".
*/


